<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Somme (river)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as River Somme</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Somme is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, flowing about 245 km west through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a> past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-quentin">Saint-Quentin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Amiens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbeville">Abbeville</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>. Known in antiquity as the Samara, it gave its name to the Gallic town of Samarobriva, later Amiens. Its valley was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-somme">Battle of the Somme</a> in 1916 and of heavy fighting in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/somme-river.jpg" alt="Somme (river)" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Donarreiskoffer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Somme.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Chlodio took Cambrai and the land up to the <b>Somme</b>, and Childeric I, father of Clovis, appears both as a king of the Franks and as a holder of Roman authority in Belgica Secunda, as Bishop Remigius of Reims implied when he wrote to Clovis on his accession.</blockquote><a href="/empire/franks">Franks · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1916, Verdun and the <b>Somme</b> together cost roughly 300,000 German dead without breakthrough.</blockquote><a href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…World War the United Kingdom mobilised millions of men, at first by volunteering and from 1916 by conscription in Great Britain, though never in Ireland; the battles of the <b>Somme</b> and Passchendaele cost hundreds of thousands of casualties, and more than 700,000 servicemen from the United Kingdom died.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Manfred von Richthofen, credited with 80 victories, was killed while pursuing an enemy aircraft over the <b>Somme</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-21">21 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Operation Michael struck British lines on the <b>Somme</b> after a five-hour bombardment, gaining more ground in days than any attack since 1914.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-21">21 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Their oppidum of Samarobriva, the bridge on the <b>Samara</b> or Somme, controlled a key crossing.</blockquote><a href="/state/ambiani">Ambiani</a></li></ul></section>
